# Heap sized for the COVERAGE-INSTRUMENTED compile, which is the worst case this build has and
# is what CI runs too. Measured 2026-07-28 by bisecting a full `clean; coverage;
# <every module>/Test/compile`:
#
#   8g  -> OutOfMemoryError in dotty.tools.dotc.transform.InstrumentCoverage
#   9g  -> passes  (the floor; 10g chosen for headroom, since the cliff is 1g wide and CI
#          runners differ from a dev Mac)
#   11g, 14g, 20g -> pass
#
# Xms is 1g, chosen by hand. It is NOT measured: GC logging could not be got into the JVM that
# does the compiling (sbt reuses a server process whose options are fixed at startup, so -Xlog
# via .jvmopts, SBT_OPTS and -J were all ignored alike). To put it on evidence, observe a
# genuinely cold compile with -Xlog:gc and size Xms from the post-GC live set; a low Xms trades
# committed memory for heap growth during the build.
-Xmx10g
-Xms1g
-Xss8M
-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8
